  "what did he ship?": {
    "answer": "He shipped a site where the agent answers from his personal Obsidian knowledge base, the notes he keeps about his own work. - The graph runs without a checkpointer, using a Postgres saver that costs 20 to 50 milliseconds per write. - When every model provider fails, the answer degrades rather than erroring, returning the retrieved source paragraph unsummarised. - The rate limit has a known ceiling, with a per-IP token budget held in memory, counting per warm instance on serverless. - The evaluation suite has no LLM judge, using 26 cases with known correct behaviour and assertions that are substring and route checks. - The site uses a vector database, Neon Postgres with pgvector, holding 82 passages under a real HNSW index on vector_cosine_ops, rebuilt on every deploy. - The site refuses to ship claims it cannot support, with an automated link checker, facts gate, token linter, and an audit of 107 structural checks.",
