  "which roles fit his experience, and what work supports that fit?": {
    "answer": "Agentic AI Engineer, Applied AI Engineer, LLM Engineer, AI Platform Engineer, and Context Engineer fit his experience. He leads the entire backend for EST's field-service platform, and the part he architected that matters most is scheduling: technicians make recurring visits to many sites for many clients, so the system has to decide who goes where and when, every time. His idempotent recurrence engine generates those visits, and turns the legacy system's silent missed jobs into dispatch alerts. He also architected the agentic SDLC harness that holds Claude Code agents to the same gates as human engineers in a regulated client codebase: least-privilege permissions, context-routing hooks, and CodeRabbit review linked to Linear through the Model Context Protocol, shipped as a plugin.",
