  "how does retrieval work here, and what tradeoffs did he make?": {
    "answer": "He uses hybrid retrieval combining BM25 keyword search with dense cosine vector search, fusing ranks via reciprocal rank fusion at k=60, skipping embedding calls when the top BM25 score exceeds 2.2 times the runner-up, and breaking ties by selecting the better single rank rather than corpus order. The tradeoff worth asking about is that hybrid retrieval costs more per query than dense-only because dense embeddings compress meaning and lose surface form, causing misses on exact terms like client names, project codes, and document titles in the consulting corpus, which he deemed worth the cost.",
